- **Avoid excessive DOM size** (reduces E on the client): the page no longer builds one row per client in the live DOM. It shows 100 rows at a time, so the browser keeps a small tree to lay out and paint, however many clients the API returns. In Green Metrics Tool micro-benchmarks, 30 page loads of a 10,000-row table with 14 elements per row used about 56% less CPU energy when paginated to 100 rows as a plain `<table>` built in a `DocumentFragment`. That was about 457 J against about 1036 J.
