- **CSS `@keyframes` instead of a JS-driven animation** (reduces E): the browser runs the shimmer itself, with no script callback on every frame. In Green Metrics Tool micro-benchmarks (20-second animation in a real browser), CSS `@keyframes` used about 145 J of CPU energy and a JavaScript `requestAnimationFrame` version about 161 J, roughly 10% less.
