```javascript
// eval-viewer.js: triage view for nightly eval runs
async function loadPredictions(runId) {
  const res = await fetch(`/api/eval-runs/${runId}/predictions`);
  const preds = await res.json(); // [{id, file, label, predicted, confidence}, ...]
  document.getElementById("run-title").textContent = `Run ${runId}`;
  renderTable(preds);
}

function renderTable(preds) {
  const minConf = parseFloat(document.getElementById("min-conf").value);
  const onlyWrong = document.getElementById("only-wrong").checked;
  const tbody = document.querySelector("#pred-table tbody");
  tbody.innerHTML = "";

  const rows = preds
    .filter(p => p.confidence >= minConf)
    .filter(p => !onlyWrong || p.label !== p.predicted)
    .sort((a, b) => a.confidence > b.confidence);

  for (const p of rows) {
    const tr = document.createElement("tr");
    tr.className = p.label === p.predicted ? "ok" : "miss";
    tr.innerHTML = `
      <td><div class="cell"><span class="mono">${p.id}</span></div></td>
      <td><div class="cell"><a href="/samples/${p.file}" target="_blank">${p.file}</a></div></td>
      <td><div class="cell"><span class="tag">${p.label}</span></div></td>
      <td><div class="cell"><span class="tag">${p.predicted}</span></div></td>
      <td><div class="cell">
        <div class="bar" style="width:${(p.confidence * 100).toFixed(1)}%"></div>
        <span>${p.confidence.toFixed(3)}</span>
      </div></td>`;
    tr.addEventListener("click", () => openSample(p));
    tbody.appendChild(tr);
    document.getElementById("count").textContent = `${tbody.children.length} predictions`;
  }
}

document.getElementById("min-conf").addEventListener("input", () => renderTable(window.preds));
document.getElementById("only-wrong").addEventListener("change", () => renderTable(window.preds));
```

**Workload:** web (internal ML triage tool, 12,000 rows per run)

#### [Bug] Filters crash after the first render
- **Where:** the two `addEventListener` calls at the bottom
- **Issue:** `loadPredictions` keeps `preds` in a local variable, so `window.preds` is never set. Moving the slider calls `renderTable(undefined)`, which throws a `TypeError` on `.filter`.
- **Fix:** store the data in a module-level variable and filter from it (see the code below).

#### [Bug] Sort order is not reliable
- **Where:** `.sort((a, b) => a.confidence > b.confidence)`
- **Issue:** the comparator returns `true`/`false`, which become `1`/`0` and are never negative. `Array.prototype.sort` needs a negative, zero or positive number, so "least confident first" is not guaranteed.
- **Fix:** `.sort((a, b) => a.confidence - b.confidence)`.

#### [Security] Upload filenames go into `innerHTML`
- **Where:** `${p.file}` in the row template
- **Issue:** the filenames come from production uploads. A name like `<img src=x onerror=...>.jpg` runs script in the browser of everyone on the ML team.
- **Fix:** build cells with `textContent`, and put the filename in the URL through `encodeURIComponent`.

#### [High] All 12,000 rows go into the live DOM, one by one
- **Where:** the `for` loop in `renderTable`
- **Issue:** each row has about 17 elements (5 `div.cell` wrappers plus spans), so one render creates around 200,000 elements. Every row is appended to the live `tbody`, and the counter is rewritten for every row. The slider fires `input` many times per second, and each event rebuilds the entire table. That causes the slow first paint, the lag and the fan noise.
- **Fix:** filter and sort the whole array as before, but render only one page of 100 rows. Use plain cells, build the page in a `DocumentFragment`, and set the counter once:
  ```javascript
  const PAGE_SIZE = 100;
  let allPreds = [];
  let visible = [];
  let page = 0;

  async function loadPredictions(runId) {
    const res = await fetch(`/api/eval-runs/${runId}/predictions`);
    if (!res.ok) throw new Error(`eval run ${runId}: HTTP ${res.status}`);
    allPreds = await res.json(); // [{id, file, label, predicted, confidence}, ...]
    document.getElementById("run-title").textContent = `Run ${runId}`;
    applyFilters();
  }

  function applyFilters() {
    const minConf = parseFloat(document.getElementById("min-conf").value);
    const onlyWrong = document.getElementById("only-wrong").checked;
    visible = allPreds
      .filter(p => p.confidence >= minConf && (!onlyWrong || p.label !== p.predicted))
      .sort((a, b) => a.confidence - b.confidence);
    page = 0;
    renderPage();
  }

  function cell(tr, text) {
    const td = tr.insertCell();
    td.textContent = text;
    return td;
  }

  function renderPage() {
    const start = page * PAGE_SIZE;
    const frag = document.createDocumentFragment();
    for (const p of visible.slice(start, start + PAGE_SIZE)) {
      const tr = document.createElement("tr");
      tr.className = p.label === p.predicted ? "ok" : "miss";
      cell(tr, p.id);
      const link = document.createElement("a");
      link.href = `/samples/${encodeURIComponent(p.file)}`;
      link.target = "_blank";
      link.textContent = p.file;
      tr.insertCell().append(link);
      cell(tr, p.label);
      cell(tr, p.predicted);
      const conf = cell(tr, p.confidence.toFixed(3));
      conf.className = "conf";
      conf.style.setProperty("--conf", p.confidence);
      tr.addEventListener("click", () => openSample(p));
      frag.append(tr);
    }
    document.querySelector("#pred-table tbody").replaceChildren(frag);
    const pages = Math.max(1, Math.ceil(visible.length / PAGE_SIZE));
    document.getElementById("count").textContent =
      `${visible.length} predictions, page ${page + 1} of ${pages}`;
    document.getElementById("prev").disabled = page === 0;
    document.getElementById("next").disabled = page >= pages - 1;
  }

  document.getElementById("min-conf").addEventListener("input", applyFilters);
  document.getElementById("only-wrong").addEventListener("change", applyFilters);
  document.getElementById("prev").addEventListener("click", () => { page--; renderPage(); });
  document.getElementById("next").addEventListener("click", () => { page++; renderPage(); });
  ```
  A CSS gradient on the cell replaces the separate bar element:
  ```css
  #pred-table td.conf {
    background: linear-gradient(to right, #d6e4f0 calc(var(--conf) * 100%), transparent 0);
  }
  ```
  You will need two buttons, `#prev` and `#next`, next to the table.
- **Impact:** E on every reviewer's machine, on every load and every slider move. Each slider tick now rebuilds 100 rows instead of up to 12,000. In Green Metrics Tool measurements, 30 page loads of a 10,000-row table with 14 elements per row, appended to the live DOM one by one, used about 56% less CPU energy after paginating to 100 rows per page as a plain `<table>` built in a `DocumentFragment`.
- **Behavior change:** filtering and sorting still cover all predictions. The difference is that browser find (Ctrl+F) now searches only the current page.

