**Workload:** web (internal viewer, client-side rendering)

#### [Security] Run name is inserted as HTML
- **Where:** `document.getElementById('title').innerHTML = ...`
- **Issue:** `data.run_name` comes from the run file. If it contains markup, the page runs it. Run files can be uploaded by other people.
- **Fix:** use `textContent`.

#### [High] Every peak is rendered at once, with two wrapper elements per cell
- **Where:** the `data.peaks.forEach(...)` loop
- **Issue:** a run with about 12k peaks creates about 130k DOM nodes (a row, plus a `div` and a `span` for each of 5 cells). Each row is also parsed from an HTML string and appended to the live DOM one at a time. The browser has to build, style and lay out all of it, even though only a few dozen rows are visible.
- **Fix:** keep the data in an array and show one page of 100 rows. Use a plain `<table>` with one `td` per value, and build each page in a `DocumentFragment`.
- **Impact:** reduces client E and M for every page load. In Green Metrics Tool micro-benchmarks, 30 page loads of a 10,000-row table built from 14 elements per row used about 56% less CPU energy when paginated to 100 rows per page as a plain table in a `DocumentFragment`.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>Peak list viewer</title>
<style>
  td { padding: 4px 12px; border-bottom: 1px solid #ddd; text-align: right; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<h3 id="title"></h3>
<p>
  <button id="prev">Prev</button>
  <span id="page"></span>
  <button id="next">Next</button>
</p>
<table><tbody id="peaks"></tbody></table>
<script>
const PAGE_SIZE = 100;
let peaks = [];
let page = 0;

function render() {
  const pages = Math.max(1, Math.ceil(peaks.length / PAGE_SIZE));
  const start = page * PAGE_SIZE;
  const frag = document.createDocumentFragment();
  for (const p of peaks.slice(start, start + PAGE_SIZE)) {
    const tr = document.createElement('tr');
    const values = [
      p.mz.toFixed(4),
      p.intensity.toExponential(2),
      p.charge,
      p.rt.toFixed(2),
      p.snr.toFixed(1),
    ];
    for (const v of values) {
      const td = document.createElement('td');
      td.textContent = v;
      tr.appendChild(td);
    }
    frag.appendChild(tr);
  }
  document.getElementById('peaks').replaceChildren(frag);
  document.getElementById('page').textContent = (page + 1) + ' / ' + pages;
  document.getElementById('prev').disabled = page === 0;
  document.getElementById('next').disabled = page >= pages - 1;
}

document.getElementById('prev').onclick = () => { page--; render(); };
document.getElementById('next').onclick = () => { page++; render(); };

fetch('/api/runs/latest/peaks.json')
  .then(r => r.json())
  .then(data => {
    document.getElementById('title').textContent =
      'Run: ' + data.run_name + ' (' + data.peaks.length + ' peaks)';
    peaks = data.peaks;
    render();
  });
</script>
</body>
</html>
```

