- **Issue:** your friend is only partly right. In Green Metrics Tool micro-benchmarks of a small booking page, an esbuild minified build (`--minify --drop:console`) used about 2% less client CPU energy than the unminified sources. That is within measurement noise. For a file this small, minification does not save measurable CPU in the browser. It saves bytes on the network, which helps shoppers on slow mobile connections a little.
