```javascript
// report-client.js - inlined into report.html by lint-report.js
// messages: [{ file, line, col, ruleId, severity, message }]
const PAGE_SIZE = 100;
const messages = window.__LINT_MESSAGES__;
const tbody = document.getElementById('rows');
const filter = document.getElementById('severity');
const countEl = document.getElementById('count');

// Pager controls, created here so the CLI template stays unchanged.
const pager = document.createElement('div');
pager.id = 'pager';
const prev = document.createElement('button');
prev.type = 'button';
prev.textContent = 'Previous';
const next = document.createElement('button');
next.type = 'button';
next.textContent = 'Next';
const label = document.createElement('span');
pager.append(prev, label, next);
tbody.closest('table').after(pager);

let visible = messages;
let page = 0;

function render() {
  const pages = Math.max(1, Math.ceil(visible.length / PAGE_SIZE));
  const start = page * PAGE_SIZE;
  const frag = document.createDocumentFragment();

  for (const m of visible.slice(start, start + PAGE_SIZE)) {
    const tr = document.createElement('tr');
    const cols = [
      [m.file, 'file'],
      [m.line + ':' + m.col, 'pos'],
      [m.ruleId || '-', 'rule'],
      [m.severity, 'sev'],
      [m.message, 'msg'],
    ];
    for (const [text, cls] of cols) {
      const td = document.createElement('td');
      td.className = 'cell ' + cls;
      td.textContent = text;
      tr.appendChild(td);
    }
    frag.appendChild(tr);
  }

  tbody.replaceChildren(frag);
  countEl.textContent = visible.length + ' messages';
  label.textContent = ' Page ' + (page + 1) + ' of ' + pages + ' ';
  prev.disabled = page === 0;
  next.disabled = page >= pages - 1;
}

function applyFilter() {
  const wanted = filter.value;
  visible = wanted === 'all'
    ? messages
    : messages.filter((m) => m.severity === wanted);
  page = 0;
  render();
}

prev.addEventListener('click', () => { page--; render(); });
next.addEventListener('click', () => { page++; render(); });
filter.addEventListener('change', applyFilter);
applyFilter();
```

**Green Notes**
- **Paginate the table** (reduces E): the old code built one row for every message, so a 30k-message run put a huge tree into the live DOM. Now only 100 rows exist at a time, and the filter and the counter still work on the full list. In Green Metrics Tool micro-benchmarks, a 10,000-row table with wrappers around every cell, appended row by row, used about 56% less client CPU energy (30 page loads) when it was paginated to 100 rows per page as a plain table. Your numbers will differ, but the cause is the same: less DOM to build, style and lay out.
- **No wrapper elements** (reduces E): each row had about 21 elements (`tr`, 5 `td`, and a `div`, `div` and `span` in each cell). Now it has 6. The `cell` and column classes sit directly on the `td`.
- **Build rows in a `DocumentFragment`** (reduces E): the page is updated once per render, not once per row.

Things to check:
- The counter shows the total number of filtered messages, not the rows on screen. Before, it showed the same number, because every row was on screen.
- Your CSS may style `.cell-wrap`. Those rules are no longer needed, and `.cell`, `.file`, `.pos` and so on now apply to the `td`. Any `.cell span` selector should change to `td.cell`.
- Browser search (Ctrl+F) only finds text on the current page now. If people rely on that, tell them to use the severity filter, or add a text filter to `applyFilter`.

