**Green Notes**
- **CSS keyframes instead of a JS animation loop** (reduces E): the page runs this animation for minutes, so per-frame JS work adds up. The animation only changes `transform`, and the browser runs it without calling your code on every frame. In Green Metrics Tool micro-benchmarks of a 20-second animation, CSS `@keyframes` used about 10% less CPU energy than a `requestAnimationFrame` loop with style updates.

No loop needed. Keyframes are out, but CSS can still do the smoothing. JS sets a custom property when new data arrives, about 10 times a second. A CSS transition fills the gap between updates.

