hello, we run a small int8 model on a CPU server for sensor classification and this is the step before the model. it quantize the float features for every request. my colleague say numba make it much faster and so it will save energy. how much energy we will save if we add it? we have maybe 3 million request per day, every request has some thousand features.

```python
import numpy as np

def quantize_input(x, scale, zero_point):
    out = np.empty(len(x), dtype=np.int8)
    for i in range(len(x)):
        q = int(round(x[i] / scale)) + zero_point
        if q < -128:
            q = -128
        elif q > 127:
            q = 127
        out[i] = q
    return out

def predict(model, features, scale, zero_point):
    qx = quantize_input(features, scale, zero_point)
    return model.run(qx)
```

