**Green Notes**
- **Remove unused CSS** (reduces network): the page has about 40 lines of CSS and every rule is used. I did not add a CSS framework, because it would ship thousands of rules for a page that needs a few. In Green Metrics Tool measurements of 50 cold page loads, purging a 16 KB stylesheet to 0.75 KB changed client energy by only about 2%, which is within noise. So the gain here is fewer bytes on real networks, not CPU. For a one-page site that is enough.
- **Inline CSS, no JavaScript:** the browser needs one request for the whole page. This is fine for a single page. If you add more pages later, move the CSS to a shared file so it can be cached.
- **System font stack:** no font files to download.
